WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.703 --> 00:00:02.473
- [Narrator] It's a small
comfort that we're not alone

00:00:02.473 --> 00:00:05.785
in our fear of the dark or
even of our own shadows.

00:00:05.785 --> 00:00:08.785
Wherever we go, a small
bit of darkness follows us.

00:00:08.785 --> 00:00:10.414
Whether it's a natural effect of light

00:00:10.414 --> 00:00:13.293
or something more sinister
remains uncertain.

00:00:13.293 --> 00:00:15.613
This October, on Friday the 13th,

00:00:15.613 --> 00:00:18.482
from an executive producer
of The Walking Dead

00:00:18.482 --> 00:00:21.034
and an executive producer of The X-Files

00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:22.808
comes six terrifying tales based on

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:25.312
the podcast phenomenon, Lore.

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:27.742
Until then, we offer you this short film

00:00:27.742 --> 00:00:29.659
inspired by the series.

00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:36.308
- The worlds of shadow and light

00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:38.932
can be very frightening for children.

00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:39.816
(thunder rumbling)

00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:44.638
I'm Dr. Michelle Golland, and
I'm a clinical psychologist.

00:00:44.638 --> 00:00:46.279
We all have a shadow.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:50.446
We have dark parts, we have
aggression, we have impulses

00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:53.226
that can hurt people.

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:55.306
- [Narrator] Carl Jung
referred to the shadow

00:00:55.306 --> 00:00:57.407
as the darker parts of ourselves.

00:00:57.407 --> 00:01:01.068
The part we keep safely
hidden by our conscience mind.

00:01:01.068 --> 00:01:03.049
But for some, the shadow
is an all-together

00:01:03.049 --> 00:01:05.192
real embodiment of evil.

00:01:05.192 --> 00:01:07.525
One that goes by many names.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:13.389
- I think when we talk about
shadow and shadow people,

00:01:13.389 --> 00:01:16.881
we're inherently talking
about psychology and our soul.

00:01:16.881 --> 00:01:20.298
A spiritual sense that there is something

00:01:21.885 --> 00:01:24.704
beyond the physical realm.

00:01:24.704 --> 00:01:26.584
- [Narrator] An obsession
with the shadow realm

00:01:26.584 --> 00:01:28.278
is what fueled the depraved desires

00:01:28.278 --> 00:01:31.108
of 15th century nobleman, Gilles de Rais,

00:01:31.108 --> 00:01:33.647
who lured little children
to an unthinkable doom

00:01:33.647 --> 00:01:37.208
behind the walls of his castle
and the French countryside.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:39.859
An avowed fan of de Rais'
perverted handiwork,

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:42.167
Edward Paisnel, the Beast of Jersey,

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.002
terrorized the Isle of
Wight from the early 1960s

00:01:45.002 --> 00:01:47.169
until his capture in 1971.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.832
Donning a rubber mask,
Paisnel broke into homes

00:01:51.832 --> 00:01:53.608
to attack 13 women and children

00:01:53.608 --> 00:01:56.275
as they lay innocently sleeping.

00:01:57.619 --> 00:01:59.906
It is the echoes of
haunting stories like these

00:01:59.906 --> 00:02:02.621
that inspired the deadly
myth of the Slenderman,

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:05.100
a tall figure who is said
to reach through computers

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.855
to beckon his victims out
of the safety of their homes

00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:11.039
and into the darkness of the woods.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:15.929
- It's a vanishing story and
who hasn't wanted to vanish?

00:02:15.929 --> 00:02:20.131
But then also, how scary if you're taken.

00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:22.164
- [Narrator] His choice
of attire is appropriately

00:02:22.164 --> 00:02:25.183
the dark suit and tie
favored by undertakers.

00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:28.339
Though unlike his contemporaries,
to look into his face

00:02:28.339 --> 00:02:31.895
is to stare into a pale, featureless void

00:02:31.895 --> 00:02:35.024
that drives survivors to
the brink of insanity.

00:02:35.024 --> 00:02:36.657
But can these shadow people really be

00:02:36.657 --> 00:02:40.060
the physical embodiment of
evil from the world beyond?

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.119
Or are they just a story we tell ourselves

00:02:42.119 --> 00:02:45.692
to cope with the darkness
that lives within us all?

00:02:45.692 --> 00:02:50.196
- We develop shadows
from the time we're born.

00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:52.527
And it's a defense system.

00:02:52.527 --> 00:02:55.716
The shadow people are the embodiment

00:02:55.716 --> 00:02:58.299
of these defenses that we have.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:03.104
- [Narrator] Our innermost
fears and twisted curiosities,

00:03:03.104 --> 00:03:06.900
it seems, will arrive at
one of two conclusions.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.173
We are the leery prey of the shadows

00:03:09.173 --> 00:03:11.756
or we stalk the prey with them.

